      "mergeID": "5c3ce579f328106c82676038",
      "mergedPostDetails": "With the ability to check people's avatar stats, it's not unusual for me to see avatars with directional lights on them in order to enable the depth buffer. I've seen a pokemon that can vomit decals on the floor, Reinheart from Overwatch with a proper shield shader, pettable goats, and many tri-planar shader avatars.\n\nEach one of these avatars have a directional light to enable the depth buffer, and it's hurting performance a bunch by globally adding an extra draw-call per-object per-directional light!\n\nCan we either just enable the depth-buffer, or add a component to avatars that request to enable the depth buffer?",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Enable Depth Buffer by default",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5b81460765c59b7bc1fafb34",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Depth buffer itself is costly. It adds 2x drawcalls even if the light doesn't affect anything and doesn't cast the shadows on any object. It is up to the world creator to decide if the world needs it or not",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
