      "value": "@{5a766b8a0868b44b53569ce4|full_name} I might have misworded what I meant by this, and by that I mean there are prefabs and shader systems that use dedicated light sources to distort meshes, the popular examples would be something like DPS where a certain threshold would either make the mesh shrink or bend the mesh in a certain way like a collider would. What I was trying to say here is that VRC *should* make their own dedicated depth texture that is constantly on because if they change the in game default behavior my fear/concern is that it would break how some things function. having something like a _VRCDepthTexture and even _VRCDepthNormals in various situations would be more helpful as well as keeping the default behavior of the _CameraDepthTexture",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
